{"pageProps":{"meta":{"id":"obsidian:minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test-en","title":"MiniMax H3-Image Test: 64GB Mac can natively produce 4K—how long does it take to modify reference images?","date":"2026-11-11","updated":"2026-11-13","summary":"Running the community 4-bit version on the M5 Pro 64GB Mac: 2K raw image takes about 73 seconds, native 4K about 6 minutes 17 seconds. Compare the original images edited with single and dual images and memory records to see which tasks are suitable for them.","categories":[{"id":"markdown-category-0-新锐模型","name":"新锐模型","color":"default"}],"categoryNames":["新锐模型"],"tags":[{"id":"markdown-tag-0-Local deployment","name":"Local deployment","color":"default"},{"id":"markdown-tag-1-LocalBrain","name":"LocalBrain","color":"default"}],"image":"/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/cover-fe9144cf14.jpg","coverBlockId":null,"slug":"minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test-en","legacyPaths":[],"lang":"en","translationOf":"minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test","articleType":"model","discoveryName":"MiniMax H3-Image","discoveryCategory":"图片生成","discoveryStage":"本地实测","discoveryUrl":"https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3-Image","source":"markdown","fixedProductFooter":true},"markdownHtml":"<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Info: Machine translation</strong>\nThis post was machine-translated from the Chinese original. Wording may be rough in places — the <a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"website\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://hyphentech.top/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/\">Chinese version</a> is authoritative.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Summary</strong>\nRunning the community 4-bit version on the M5 Pro 64GB Mac: 2K raw image takes about 73 seconds, native 4K about 6 minutes 17 seconds. Compare the original images edited with single and dual images and memory records to see which tasks are suitable for them.\nNovember 11, 2026 · Let AI be your superpower</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The first task I gave MiniMax H3-Image was to have it draw a lakeside glass greenhouse: a red canoe on the water, with morning mist blocking a bit of the view. Then, I returned the newly generated image to the model and asked it to change the boat to yellow and add a moon. Finally, I pushed the size to 4096×4096. Dimensions and usage time were checked against the finished product and logs; Whether the image was good or correct, the images had to be viewed together.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-text-4k-5aa3f29499.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/1baba249d7c866d69c9e3eee-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/1baba249d7c866d69c9e3eee-1280.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-text-4k-5aa3f29499.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | Native 4096×4096 Example: Walnut Shell Observatory. The webpage image has been reduced, with pixel-level details at the center of the original image attached.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1600\"></picture></a></p>\n<h2>Native 4K works well, and editors can indeed make changes</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Local tasks</th>\n<th>Finished product dimensions</th>\n<th>End-to-end time-consuming</th>\n<th>Graphical calculation peak</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Pure text generates images</td>\n<td>2048×2048</td>\n<td>72.6 seconds</td>\n<td>24.46 GiB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Edited with only reference images</td>\n<td>2048×2048</td>\n<td>191.4 seconds</td>\n<td>25.21 GiB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pure text generates images</td>\n<td>4096×4096</td>\n<td>376.9 seconds</td>\n<td>24.46 GiB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dual reference chart combinations</td>\n<td>2048×2048</td>\n<td>341.7 seconds</td>\n<td>25.27 GiB</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<blockquote>\n<p>M5 Pro, 64 GiB unified memory, macOS 26.7.1; each item is used once, independent process, system file cache not cleared. Time consumption includes encoding, sampling, decoding, and disk writing.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>In 4K images, cracks on wooden shells, brass binoculars, and star map textures can all be recognized. Once you place them at webpage width, these details are easily suppressed. Here’s a direct crop of the original image area to help judge whether 4K is useful for this type of still life.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-text-4k-detail-7a39797bed.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/4c439e41e0aff95c30f46097-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/4c439e41e0aff95c30f46097-1024.webp 1024w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-text-4k-detail-7a39797bed.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | 4096×4096 Partial view of the original image, not enlarged or sharpened after capture.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\"></picture></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-text-2k-d52b9be372.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/d770273d6c343e57aec90764-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/d770273d6c343e57aec90764-1280.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-text-2k-d52b9be372.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | Single Image Editing: Red Canoe, Lake Surface, and Greenhouse.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1600\"></picture></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-edit-2k-d3b906ea97.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/66043f494f7f72ef2f5ee559-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/66043f494f7f72ef2f5ee559-1280.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-edit-2k-d3b906ea97.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | After editing a single image: the ship turns yellow and the moon appears; The composition is largely preserved, but lighting and local details change.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1600\"></picture></a></p>\n<p>If you just want to change colors and add a distinct element to a picture, this set of editing results is already useful. Once the position is accurate, you need to leave time for review. In the dual-image task, I had it place the Walnut Shell Observatory on the bridge in front of the greenhouse; The main elements of both images were included in the finished product, but the observatory was placed on the left side of the image and wasn’t placed accurately on the bridge. For tasks that require strict retention of position, text, or pixel level, I still use layer compositing to finish.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-edit-multi-2k-bc48a6332f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/a5eac85bc124469a02cd83af-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/a5eac85bc124469a02cd83af-1280.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-edit-multi-2k-bc48a6332f.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | Dual Reference Image Output: Theme combination successful, but the specified placement position is not fully followed.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1600\"></picture></a></p>\n<h2>With a weight of 54.5 GB, why is the measured peak graphics about 25 GiB?</h2>\n<p>Disk size and peak operation are two separate accounts. 54.5 GB is the full package size for the community four-bit version, which includes a text encoder, sampling trunk, and decoder. The adaptation implements phased component calls and performs four-bit quantization for some linear and embedded layers; Not all layers become four-bit. The measurement is the peak value of the MLX graphical calculation allocation and cannot be directly used as full-machine memory usage, nor can it be inferred that a 32GB machine can run on this basis. The system swap space did not increase during the four tasks; switching occupation already existed before machine testing.</p>\n<p>The most obvious cost after increasing the size is time. From 2048 to 4096, width and height double, pixels quadruple; The time to generate text images for these two rounds dropped from 72.6 seconds to 376.9 seconds, about 5.2 times. Both times are six steps, so single-step 4K sampling is still much more expensive. I first use 2K to set composition, color, and camera feel, preserving the image before producing in 4K. Using the same prompt to resize and resample may change the composition, so you need to take another look at the finished image.</p>\n<h2>After connecting to LocalBrain, how do you choose?</h2>\n<p>LocalBrain 2.3.4 integrates MiniMax H3-Image into the image generation category in “Discovery.” This model entry only supports Macs running macOS 26 or later with Apple chips; The Windows and Linux installation packages on the same version do not include this model feature. Full weights are already available for reuse. In “Dialog → Local Multimedia Tools → Raw Images,” select the model, choose the size, add reference images, and then edit according to the command. “Edit Image” also allows you to select the cover image and other reference images. Installation package see <a href=\"https://github.com/HackerChi-Hub/localbrain-releases/releases/tag/v2.3.4\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"download\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://github.com/HackerChi-Hub/localbrain-releases/releases/tag/v2.3.4\">LocalBrain 2.3.4 release page</a>, validation values see <a href=\"https://github.com/HackerChi-Hub/localbrain-releases\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"website\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://github.com/HackerChi-Hub/localbrain-releases\">download instructions</a>.</p>\n<p>To confirm that it really works after connecting, I ran another set using candidate installation packages and verified models from the external drive: Mr. became a blue teacup, then handed this image to the editing portal and changed it to red. Both times I got the original images 2048×2048; The former reloaded seed 0, the latter reread seed 19. The cup body pattern, window frame, and wooden table positions are well preserved. This set changed the prompts and disk environment, and the time usage was not directly compared with the table above.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-app-blue-cup-e9a2ab1969.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/12caff386ea877825b07c7b7-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/12caff386ea877825b07c7b7-1280.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-app-blue-cup-e9a2ab1969.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | LocalBrain candidate installation package reuses weights from external drives to generate blue teacups.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1600\"></picture></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-app-red-cup-141d2eb8ec.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/a28cf7641dd62dd0423d9b6d-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/a28cf7641dd62dd0423d9b6d-1280.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-app-red-cup-141d2eb8ec.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | Editing path for the same candidate installation package: Change the blue cup to the red cup, keeping the main composition.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1600\"></picture></a></p>\n<p>Size can be preset or customized. Currently, the adapter requires width and height to be integer multiples of 32, with a single side from 32 to 8192, total pixels not exceeding 20 million, and the longest side not exceeding eight times the short side. If you fill in an error, it will be prompted first; Do not secretly change the request to low resolution. Requests below about 4.2 million pixels will first be generated on the internal canvas and then output according to the request size. 2K and 4K square images have been tested; Being able to fill in the legal size does not mean every scale and memory configuration has already been tested.</p>\n<p>The official team also has a separate <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3-Image-PE\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"website\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3-Image-PE\">prompt expansion model</a>, about 17.9 GB each. Disabled by default, but both raw and modified images can be enabled after selecting the local directory. Tested with the “Blue Ceramic Teacup on the Wooden Table by the Window,” it added lighting, glaze, coaster, and desktop materials; Expansion took about 73 seconds, and the whole image took about 210 seconds. Then replaced with a red cup in Chinese language; expansion with reference image took about 162 seconds, full editing took about 484 seconds. Both finished images were specified 2496×1664; the original short sentence, actual expansion, and seed were all kept in the receipt. If you want to save time or already have a finely written prompt, just keep the default closed option.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-pe-blue-cup-d7f2314313.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/31b7025637ca119720503508-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/31b7025637ca119720503508-1280.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-pe-blue-cup-d7f2314313.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | Official expansion activated, short Chinese prompt generates 2496×1664 horizontal images.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1067\"></picture></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-pe-red-cup-335b0faa05.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"article-image-link\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/media-previews/176ca26b4e8ec7b367708101-640.webp 640w, /media-previews/176ca26b4e8ec7b367708101-1280.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1000px\"><img src=\"https://hyphentech.top/obsidian-assets/minimax-h3-image-mac-64gb-local-test/image-pe-red-cup-335b0faa05.jpg\" alt=\"AI Generation | Official expansion enabled, follow Chinese instructions to change the blue cup to red; Position, window frame, and coaster basically retained.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1067\"></picture></a></p>\n<p>The four tests in the opening table use <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/nativ-community/MiniMax-H3-Image-4bit\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"website\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://huggingface.co/nativ-community/MiniMax-H3-Image-4bit\">Community MLX 4-bit version</a>, with additional prompt expansion disabled and run according to fixed six-step and guidance coefficient 1. The tests did not compare official full precision or online services, nor did they treat the upstream specification of up to sixteen reference images as standard machine tests. Community conversion continues to use <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3-Image/blob/main/LICENSE\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"website\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3-Image/blob/main/LICENSE\">MiniMax Community License</a>; Before using it for commercial projects, first verify whether your usage scenario and region comply with the terms.</p>\n<h2>Models and adaptation sources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3-Image\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"website\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3-Image\">MiniMax H3-Image Official Model Card</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://huggingface.co/nativ-community/MiniMax-H3-Image-4bit/tree/d2e36369b1ea5cfeb90bde50592a509250052172\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"website\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://huggingface.co/nativ-community/MiniMax-H3-Image-4bit/tree/d2e36369b1ea5cfeb90bde50592a509250052172\">Tested community authority fixed version</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Neywa-Labs/mlx-vlm/pull/2702\" class=\"resource-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" data-link-kind=\"website\" title=\"Opens in a new tab · https://github.com/Neywa-Labs/mlx-vlm/pull/2702\">Apple Chip Native Operation Adaptation Records</a></li>\n</ul>\n","relatedPosts":[{"id":"obsidian:local-llm-hardware-guide-20261031","rawId":"obsidian:local-llm-hardware-guide-20261031","slug":"local-llm-hardware-guide-20261031-en","legacyPaths":[],"title":"Choosing devices in advance for Qwen4? Qwen3.8 27B, Flash-Next Local Deployment Buying Guide","date":"2026-10-31","updated":"2026-10-31","summary":"Comparing devices by capacity, bandwidth, engine, and overall cost, from 27B and Flash-Next to 9B and 4B. Attached are the 33 candidates for this issue and a snapshot of the quotes as of October 30, 2026.","categories":[{"id":"markdown-category-0-技术分享","name":"技术分享","color":"default"}],"categoryNames":["技术分享"],"tags":[{"id":"markdown-tag-0-AI","name":"AI","color":"default"},{"id":"markdown-tag-1-Local deployment","name":"Local deployment","color":"default"}],"pageCover":"/obsidian-assets/local-llm-hardware-guide-20261031/cover-880fe11d9e.jpg","cover":"/obsidian-assets/local-llm-hardware-guide-20261031/cover-880fe11d9e.jpg","source":"markdown","status":"published","lang":"en","translationOf":null,"articleType":"article","discoveryName":"为Qwen4提前选设备？Qwen3.8 27B、Flash-Next本地部署选购指南","discoveryCategory":null,"discoveryStage":null,"discoveryUrl":null,"sourcePath":"posts/local-llm-hardware-guide-20261031.md","fixedProductFooter":true},{"id":"obsidian:localbrain-h3-ltx25-video-practical-test","rawId":"obsidian:localbrain-h3-ltx25-video-practical-test","slug":"localbrain-h3-ltx25-video-practical-test-en","legacyPaths":[],"title":"H3 vs. LTX-2.5: 64GB Mac Local Video Test—How to Choose Acceleration, Transition, and Lens Control?","date":"2026-11-02","updated":"2026-11-03","summary":"Real video clips on a 64GB Mac, H3 same-topic acceleration, Transition frame start and end